## multidimensional data
Dimensional data, also known as multi-dimensional data, refers to data that can be organised and analysed in multiple dimensions or axes. This type of data is commonly used in business intelligence and data warehousing applications, where data is often stored in a multidimensional database (MDDB) or an online analytical processing (OLAP) cube.

- multidimensional data refers to data that can be organised and analysed in multiple dimensions or axes.

